From 02e57a08ad53ab704a5fe0287a021d6f3c3b0e87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michele Dipace <michele.dipace@kaffeine.net>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:39:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Fix: copying a deep drawer tree overflowed the stack

CopyEntryRecursive and CopyDirectoryRecursive kept eight PATH_MAX_LEN
buffers on the stack per level (about 10.5 KB): with the 64 KB Shell stack
the program crashed with Guru 80000003 at the sixth level, with the 256 KB
icon stack at the twenty-fifth. The $STACK:1048576 cookie in build 6 moves
the problem to about level 95, but there the overflow happens inside
dos.library and freezes the whole system without the Grim Reaper (copy of
a 150-level tree).

- the path buffers of the recursive copy, delete and count functions are
  allocated on the heap: stack use per copy level drops to about 200 bytes
- MAX_COPY_DEPTH limit for copy and counts: beyond it the copy fails
  cleanly and a move does not delete the source
- the $STACK:1048576 cookie is kept as is
---
